{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:af62ea4e24ca3cce","name":"Sinkhole","source":{"id":"source:reference-af62ea4e24ca3cce","title":"Sinkhole","revision":21440,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T01:48:20Z","sha256":"9831ccdd3ac33aaf094aee2724c2b826eb98320bded2c36239657fbe6d447107","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=21440","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Sinkhole&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-af62ea4e24ca3cce","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Unknown Regions Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Unknown_Regions_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["In your path is a large, gaping hole in the ground."]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The Sinkhole is a common Hazard. The difference between a pit and a Sinkhole is that a pit has no additional exit, whereas a Sinkhole leads to an underground passage. Despite its apparent simplicity, this Hazard can be used in many ways: a covered pit that spans a path, a deep sinkhole, a pit with spikes or other sharp objects lining the bottom, a pit with a predator at the bottom, and so on. Combatants separated by a hole can fight from different sides, or one group could attempt to force the other toward the edge.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Sinkhole Statistics (CL 4)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Keywords:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Natural"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Natural"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Trigger:"]}," A being ends its turn on a Sinkhole.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Attack:"]}," +6 vs ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Damage:"]}," 1d6 per 3 Meters (",{"tag":"a","children":["Falling Damage"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Falling_Damage","referenceId":"reference:4c0e132089e34987"},")\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Recurrence:"]}," None\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Suggested ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skills"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skills","referenceId":"reference:66d0f523a379b2de"},":"]}," The following are suggested ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skills"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skills","referenceId":"reference:66d0f523a379b2de"}," for this Hazard:\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Acrobatics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Acrobatics","referenceId":"reference:0d0b7eee2953750e"}," (DC 26):"]}," The character twists to grab the edge of the hole, gaining a +5 circumstance bonus to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"}," to avoid falling in."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Climb"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Climb","referenceId":"reference:98ca5f27d9642dc7"}," (DC 26):"]}," As the character falls into the hole, they grab the wall and slow their descent, reducing the amount of damage the character takes by half."]},"\n",{"tag":"li","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Jump"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jump","referenceId":"reference:9ee0ca3e24d60ea0"}," (DC 21):"]}," By jumping across the opening of the hole, the character gains a +2 circumstance bonus to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"}," to avoid falling in."]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Special:"]}," If the Hazard's attack against the target is successful, the target falls into the hole and takes ",{"tag":"a","children":["Falling Damage"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Falling_Damage","referenceId":"reference:4c0e132089e34987"}," when it hits the bottom.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
